  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "向儒道思想學情緒管理",
    "sub_ename": "TO LEARN EMOTIONAL MANAGEMENT FROM THE THOUGHTS OF CONFUCIANISM AND TAOISM",
    "describe_ch": "自從COVID-19至今，氣候變遷，瘟疫打亂了人類生活秩序，科技進步、只追求物質的生產力，卻忽略精神的生命力；社會價值錯亂，精神空虛徬徨，我們超越時空觀聖人；讓儒家的生命實理與道家的空靈智慧，指引我們的身、心、靈得到平衡。全世界陷入金融危機與病毒困擾，欲解決人類社會危機，惟有從儒道經典中取經；中國大陸亦在振興「國學熱」，我們豈能置身於事外？讓我們趕緊學習「雙向圓成」的儒道思想。",
    "describe_eh": "Since COVID-19, climate change and plague have disrupted the order of human life; humans only pursue technological progress and material productivity but ignore spiritual vitality. Social values are chaotic, with spiritual emptiness and hesitation. We transcend the time and space to view saints and let Confucianism and the ethereal wisdom of Taoism guide us to balance our body, mind and spirit. The world is in the grip of financial crisis and virus. To solve the crisis of human society, we can only learn from the classics of Confucianism and Taoism. Mainland China is also revitalizing the \"Chinese learning fever\". How can we stay out of it? Let us quickly learn the Confucian and Taoist thought of \"two-way perfection\".",
    "pre_subname": "",
    "pre_sub_id3": null,
    "pre_sub_ename": "",
    "pre_describe": null,
    "pre_describe_en": null,
    "scr_credit": 2.0
  },
  "targets": [
    {
      "seq": 1,
      "describe_ch": "儒家思想講「親親、仁民、愛物」；道家思想講「常善救人，故無棄人；常善救物，故無棄物。」這是最符合永續經營的生命智慧。",
      "describe_en": "Confucianism says \"close relatives, be kind to the people, and love things\"; Taoism says, \"Always be good at saving people, so no one will be abandoned; always be good at saving things, so there will be no abandonment.\" This is the wisdom of life that is most in line with sustainable management."
    },
    {
      "seq": 2,
      "describe_ch": "人人的「性」相同，故有教無類；人人的「命」不同，故因材施教。我們不是跟他人比高低，而是跟自己比進步與否，明乎此，就不會怨天尤人，才能提升身心靈的健康。",
      "describe_en": "Everyone's \"nature\" is the same, so there is no difference in teaching; everyone's \"destiny\" is different, so we should teach students according to their aptitude. We are not comparing ourselves with others, but comparing ourselves with ourselves. Only when we understand this, we will not blame others and will improve our physical and mental health."
    }
  ],
